  "goodToKnow": "Hacken means to chop: Holz hacken, Zwiebeln hacken (chop onions). Das Hackfleisch is minced meat, and Mett (raw seasoned pork) is a German favourite on bread rolls. In computing, hacken means to hack: Mein Account wurde gehackt. The Chaos Computer Club in Hamburg is one of the world's oldest and best-known hacker associations. Die Hacke is a hoe, and casually also the heel: sich die Hacken ablaufen (to run one's legs off)."
